# Forge stores and checks out every text file with LF endings.
#
# This is not a style preference. `evaluation/datasets/*/dataset.json` are hashed
# byte-for-byte in `evaluation/datasets/MANIFEST.json`, and the evaluator refuses to run
# when a hash differs (ACCURACY_VALIDATION.md §4). On a client with `core.autocrlf=true`
# — the Git for Windows default — a CRLF checkout would rewrite those bytes, so the frozen
# datasets would fail their own integrity check on a clean clone. Pinning the line ending
# keeps the manifest meaningful everywhere.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The hashed fixtures and the stored measurements are never translated, whatever the
# client's settings: they are evidence, and their bytes are the record.
evaluation/datasets/** -text
evaluation/results/** -text

# Workbooks are zip archives; never let a text filter near them.
*.xlsx binary
